WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.590
Nikhil: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.910
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.640
between Pizza Hut in the US and in India.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.973
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.280
The smallest pizza in the US
is the personal pan pizza,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.400
and it is 6 inches across.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.740
In India, our pizzas
start at personal size.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.847
It's seven inches wide
and has four slices.

00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:25.020
The US also has a small pizza,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.570
but only with the gluten-free crust,

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.470
and it is

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:30.495
difficult.

00:00:30.495 --> 00:00:33.480
10 inches wide. So depressing looking.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.740
Then we're on to the mediums.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.050
A medium pizza here in India is 10 inches

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.737
and has six slices.

00:00:38.737 --> 00:00:42.540
Joe: A US medium pizza
comes in at 12 inches wide.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.350
This medium pizza is equal
to the small pizza in the US.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.570
People in the US, sometimes
it's just really hard

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.220
not to stereotype you guys.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.370
Next up in India, we have nothing.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.560
Because medium is our largest size.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.985
That's right, we have only
two sizes, personal or medium.

00:00:58.985 --> 00:01:01.049
No large for us because

00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:05.190
Pizza Hut is watching our weight, I guess.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.600
Stereotype away, my man,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.300
because in the US, you
know we got this large,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.420
and it is 14 inches in diameter.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.920
So America's largest pizza

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.766
is 4 inches wider than India's largest.

00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:18.660
That doesn't sound so bad.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.620
However.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.080
If you calculate the surface
area of the two pizzas,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.210
those few inches make a big difference.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:28.740
The Indian medium has a surface
area of 78.5 square inches,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.240
while the US large clocks
in at 153.9 square inches.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.480
To save you from doing the
math, that's a 96% increase.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.520
That means the US large pizza

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.580
is nearly double our Indian medium.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.740
What the heck, Pizza Hut?

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.940
The type of crust you get

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.620
doesn't affect the width of the pizza,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.180
but how does it affect the value?

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.129
We're going to weigh a
medium hand-tossed slice

00:01:51.129 --> 00:01:53.190
versus a medium pan-crust slice

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.280
to see which one gives you
more pizza for your money.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.080
All right, I'm going to
do the same with our pan

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.770
and San Francisco-style
pizzas, the medium size.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.837
All right. So, medium hand-tossed weighs

00:02:04.837 --> 00:02:06.811
94 grams.

00:02:06.811 --> 00:02:08.310
Pan, the thick boy.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.390
Boy!

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.880
Whoa! 104 grams.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.202
That's a difference of --
what was the first one?

00:02:15.202 --> 00:02:18.210
That's a difference of this many grams.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:22.740
This one is pan style,
and it weighs 78 grams.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.473
This slice

00:02:25.865 --> 00:02:28.165
weighs 66 grams.

00:02:28.165 --> 00:02:29.240
Fairly lighter,

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.620
and I think this is because
when they make this pizza,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.395
they press it down into the pan,

00:02:33.395 --> 00:02:35.220
and that's the San Francisco style.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.477
This weighs more and therefore is more,

00:02:38.477 --> 00:02:39.539
'cause it's more bread.

00:02:39.539 --> 00:02:40.722
You want the cheese and the sauce.

00:02:40.722 --> 00:02:41.850
You want the fun stuff, right?

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.200
I don't -- no.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.243
Oh, boy, this is gonna be trouble.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.800
Here is everything you'll find on the menu

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.779
at Pizza Hut India that you
will not find in the US.

00:02:53.779 --> 00:02:56.802
And here are all the Pizza
Hut menu items from the US

00:02:56.802 --> 00:02:58.230
you won't find in India.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:01.140
Let's start off with the
foundation of any pizza:

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.140
the crust, starting with

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.965
the San Francisco signature style.

00:03:06.965 --> 00:03:09.240
To my understanding, it's
basically a pan pizza,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:11.928
but they press the dough
in with their hands

00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:13.290
so it's kind of hand-tossed.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.730
Next up, we have something very special.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.463
It's a Schezwan pan pizza.

00:03:19.301 --> 00:03:21.390
Oh, my God, yeah. I really like this.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.190
It's spicy. Really yum.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.450
Just to give you some comparison,

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.270
the way chicken tikka masala
was invented in the UK

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.670
but clearly inspired by Indian cuisine,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.753
Schezwan sauce was actually
invented here in Kolkata

00:03:32.753 --> 00:03:34.969
by the Chinese community
that settled down here.

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:37.437
But it's obviously inspired
by Chinese cuisine,

00:03:37.437 --> 00:03:39.660
and now it's become
part of Indian cuisine.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.200
We have accepted it wholly,
and we eat it all across India.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.960
Very exciting to see it integrated
into the Pizza Hut menu,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.020
and it actually tastes
very good on this pizza.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:53.040
Next up they have a
stuffed cheese crust Maxx,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.881
with two X's for emphasis.

00:03:55.881 --> 00:03:59.070
You can already see that this
thing is loaded with cheese.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.867
Next to the cheese, alongside it,

00:04:00.867 --> 00:04:03.210
there's, like, a sort of creamy sauce,

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.993
which Pizza Hut is calling
Peruvian creamy sauce.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.410
Whoa!

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.680
Oh, my God, yeah. This is decadent food.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.220
Next up we have a stuffed
crust with veg kebab.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.412
That's right. If you
don't know what kebab is,

00:04:18.412 --> 00:04:21.660
it's basically meat that's
cooked in a tandoor.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.980
If you don't know what a tandoor is,

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.170
please go watch the older
episodes of "Food Wars."

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.550
I've explained it eight times.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.830
A lot of people like to
leave the crust behind,

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.733
but I feel like Pizza Hut is making sure

00:04:30.733 --> 00:04:33.200
all of the pizza is eaten,
because even this looks

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.430
like a dish in itself at this point.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.200
Oh, my God, that's really yum.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.090
And the final option:

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:43.380
the stuffed crust with
a non-vegetarian kebab.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.790
Ooh.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.823
As you can see, this is what
looks to be chicken seekh.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.660
Oh, that's the best of the lot.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.140
That was amazing. Oh, my God.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.370
Smashed it, Pizza Hut.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.989
That might be the best pizza
I've had on "Food Wars" so far,

00:04:58.989 --> 00:05:00.900
and I didn't even eat the pizza part.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.905
We also have a variety of
crust options in the US,

00:05:03.905 --> 00:05:05.754
starting down here. You saw it already.

00:05:05.754 --> 00:05:07.200
Here it is again, the hand-tossed.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.020
This to me is, like,
classic. This is the default.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.310
You guys don't have hand-tossed?

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.350
Moving on: Thin 'N Crispy.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.420
I mean, how much -- look at this.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:18.240
They can't charge the same
amount for this, right?

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.140
I don't think they should.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:22.560
Moving on over here: the
original stuffed crust.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.540
They put cheese in the crust.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.684
Can you believe that?

00:05:25.684 --> 00:05:28.470
Ugh, no, it is solidified.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.329
That doesn't stop me from biting into it.

00:05:32.222 --> 00:05:34.140
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.310
Last and, let's be honest,
least: gluten-free crust.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.582
Look, I don't know what's
going on with gluten allergies,

00:05:40.582 --> 00:05:43.015
and my apologies if you have
one, but I'm looking at this,

00:05:43.015 --> 00:05:44.220
I'm just like, I'm sorry, guys.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.780
I mean, is this that much better?

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.420
I don't know how you can enjoy this.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:49.500
And for a limited time,

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.250
Pizza Hut in the US has
Detroit-style pizza!

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.808
Let's go! Let us go.

00:05:54.808 --> 00:05:56.299
Look at this. Are you
kidding me with this?

00:05:56.299 --> 00:05:58.035
Detroit-style pizza. What's Detroit style?

00:05:58.035 --> 00:06:01.320
Well, they cook it in a square
pan that has sides to it.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.755
It's like when you cook brownies

00:06:02.755 --> 00:06:06.221
and every brownie is
a corner or end piece.

00:06:06.221 --> 00:06:07.500
It's like that, for pizza.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.896
So every slice is going to have

00:06:09.896 --> 00:06:12.120
the crispy crust on the
outside. It's thicker.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.770
One of my favorite pizza styles.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.120
I'm glad Pizza Hut's doing it.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.503
Generous with the pepperoni,
guys. I appreciate it.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.080
Not the best Detroit-style
pizza I've ever had,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.490
but it's pretty good.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.250
I think they go bread,
cheese, topping, sauce.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.070
These are the toppings we
found under the categories

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.680
classic, favorites, and delight.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.090
Very arbitrarily named,

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.650
but, yeah, let's jump into it.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.950
The first option is chicken sausage.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.375
Smells really good.

00:06:38.375 --> 00:06:41.823
A lot of onions. I love onions.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.240
Mm.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:46.410
It's pretty classic.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.773
The next pizza is spiced paneer.

00:06:48.773 --> 00:06:50.520
Paneer, if you don't
know, is cottage cheese.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.163
We make it all over the
place here in India,

00:06:52.163 --> 00:06:54.240
and it's one of our favorite ingredients.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.503
We use it on everything, even pizzas.

00:06:58.586 --> 00:06:59.580
Not very spicy,

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.980
but definitely it's got,
like, a tangy twist to it.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.230
Next up we have the Veggie Feast.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:08.763
It's got some herbed onion,
capsicum, and sweet corn.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.470
This is such a wholesome, chill pizza.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.670
It's definitely a classic.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.680
It's something your
mom would make at home.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.960
Next up, we have the veggie tandoori,

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.610
which I have already taken a bite of.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.940
We got this one with the Schezwan crust,

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.244
so it's definitely spicier

00:07:24.244 --> 00:07:26.610
than the typical pan pizza you'll get.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.430
And I already tasted it,
and I told you I loved it.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:30.630
I love the spice.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.816
Next up, we have spiced
chicken meat-a-balls!

00:07:34.816 --> 00:07:36.570
It's a very straightforward pizza,

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:39.840
but we got it with the
cheese-burst filling.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.060
Next up, we have the
Chicken N Corn Delight.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.590
It already has the word
"delight" in the name,

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.386
so I'm assuming it should be a delight,

00:07:45.386 --> 00:07:46.710
but I'll be the judge of that.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:50.883
Capsicum; chicken, just
strewn across; and corn.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.012
It's got too much going on, I would say.

00:07:55.012 --> 00:07:57.720
Personally, I would not
order a pizza like this.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:07:59.220
Next up, to round it all off,

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:02.220
this is the double chicken sausage pizza.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.417
Am I wrong in saying
that this just looks like

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:07.530
a boring version of the
normal chicken sausage pizza,

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:11.250
which has onions and
just feels a lot better?

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.983
We have a pepperoni pizza

00:08:13.983 --> 00:08:15.999
that is made of pork and not chicken

00:08:15.999 --> 00:08:18.183
and a Pepperoni Lover's pizza.

00:08:18.183 --> 00:08:20.100
Which one has more pepperoni?

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:20.940
I can't tell!

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.500
The supreme pizza.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:26.849
It has pepperoni, mushrooms,
green peppers, onions,

00:08:26.849 --> 00:08:27.960
and that's it.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.180
But if that's not
supreme-y enough for you,

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:33.240
we have the super supreme,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.520
which, now they've
introduced black olives.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:37.296
Meat Lover's, baby!

00:08:37.296 --> 00:08:39.480
Meat Lover's!

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.960
You got pepperoni, you got
bacon, you got sausage.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.392
I bet there's something else on there

00:08:44.392 --> 00:08:45.608
that I don't know, another meat.

00:08:45.608 --> 00:08:47.430
I just, it's beautiful.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.610
This next pizza is the Veggie Lover's,

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.140
and I absolutely hate it.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.007
You want veggies? Go get a
salad. Don't put it on pizza.

00:08:54.007 --> 00:08:55.500
Like, you're not fooling
anyone, all right?

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.600
Backyard barbecue chicken.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.790
Yuelei, do you have enough B-roll?

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.170
I think, it's barbecue chicken,

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.840
but I think they use barbecue
sauce instead of pizza sauce.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.973
Genius. Genius!

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:09.540
This is so good.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.570
Oh, yeah! The Buffalo chicken.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.340
It's, like, surprisingly good.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.860
Pizza Hut does not have a straight

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:19.235
Hawaiian pizza on the menu.

00:09:19.235 --> 00:09:22.302
The only thing they have
is Hawaiian chicken.

00:09:22.302 --> 00:09:24.210
I see, obviously, chicken.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.902
I see a pineapple.

00:09:25.902 --> 00:09:27.727
I think I see ham? Yep.

00:09:27.727 --> 00:09:30.240
I think Hawaiian should
just be pineapple and bacon,

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.710
and if you want to throw some
chicken on it that's fine,

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.450
but if you have a strong opinion

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.970
either for or against pineapple
on pizza, you're wrong.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.230
It's a perfectly fine topping.

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:39.630
I don't know why everyone
gets so worked up about it.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.658
More pizzas, and these are all part

00:09:41.658 --> 00:09:43.736
of the signature collection.

00:09:43.736 --> 00:09:45.660
There are 11 pizzas in front of me?

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.943
Two, four, six ... ah, OK.

00:09:47.943 --> 00:09:50.153
First off, the Country Feast.

00:09:50.153 --> 00:09:52.140
It looks super saucy.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.550
It's all loaded with vegetables.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.770
There's mushrooms,
capsicum, onion, sweet corn,

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:58.596
roasted peppers; everything that you want

00:09:58.596 --> 00:10:01.413
on a country-themed pizza.

00:10:01.413 --> 00:10:03.750
All right, next up we
have tandoori paneer.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.730
If you remember in the
previous categories,

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.350
we had spiced paneer.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:09.843
So all I'm looking for
is, why is this different?

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:14.850
Oh, my God, that's really yum.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.650
Next up is the Veggie Lover.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:19.800
It's basically got
tomato, onion, capsicum,

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.855
mushrooms, and some red paprika

00:10:21.855 --> 00:10:24.243
and hopefully a whole lot of flavor.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.830
It's underwhelming. I'm gonna be honest.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.960
Next up, we have chicken tikka.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.460
Everybody knows chicken tikka.

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:35.983
It's a bit too strong, too tangy,

00:10:35.983 --> 00:10:37.212
and I think they could have gone

00:10:37.212 --> 00:10:38.970
with a thinner layer of sauce.

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:41.310
Next up we have the malai chicken tikka.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:42.930
Malai is basically cream.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.983
So malai kebabs, they
basically grill the chicken

00:10:45.983 --> 00:10:47.610
and they pour malai on top.

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:51.577
We have the chicken pepperoni.

00:10:51.577 --> 00:10:53.730
Double paneer supreme.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.670
You like paneer? You like Supreme clothes?

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.407
Well, this has double of
it, minus the clothes.

00:10:59.407 --> 00:11:01.230
Veggie supreme.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:03.660
Everybody in India has
heard of this pizza.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:04.980
This is a painting.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:08.880
I can genuinely see this on
the wall of an art gallery.

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:12.150
There's capsicum, there's
olives, there's corn,

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.997
there's onions, there's corn again.

00:11:15.997 --> 00:11:17.550
Veg Kebab Surprise.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:21.291
I'm curious to know what's
gonna be surprising about this.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.800
Surprise, surprise, it tastes bland.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:28.470
And now on to our
penultimate signature pizza.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:31.347
This is the chicken tikka supreme!

00:11:31.347 --> 00:11:32.760
Woohoo!

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:34.565
Basically what they've
done is they've taken

00:11:34.565 --> 00:11:36.415
four different kinds of chicken

00:11:36.415 --> 00:11:38.173
and they put it on a pizza.

00:11:38.173 --> 00:11:41.430
And finally, in the line
of signature pizzas,

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.820
we have Triple Chicken Feast.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:48.170
It has all of the above ingredients,

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.978
and we've also gone the extra mile

00:11:49.978 --> 00:11:53.167
and taken it with a chicken
stuffing in the crust.

00:11:53.167 --> 00:11:55.603
Overall, Pizza Hut has actually killed it.

00:11:55.603 --> 00:11:57.870
I think all the ingredients
have tasted super fresh,

00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:59.607
all the meat has also tasted really soft

00:11:59.607 --> 00:12:01.500
and juicy and delicious,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.068
and the sauce has been
consistently yum throughout.

00:12:04.068 --> 00:12:06.990
Damn, Pizza Hut. Good job.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.460
As mentioned before,

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:13.110
currently have a Detroit-style
pizza at the US Pizza Hut.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:15.000
This is what it looks like.
Two slices are missing.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.100
I skipped lunch, and
breakfast, to be honest.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.080
For those of you outside
of the United States,

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.970
Detroit is a city in Michigan.

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:23.190
They have their own style
of pizza. I really enjoy it.

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:26.044
You can also get it as
a supreme Detroit style

00:12:26.044 --> 00:12:28.530
and a meaty deluxe Detroit style.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:29.738
And I didn't get them

00:12:29.738 --> 00:12:31.500
because it all looks exactly like this.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:33.750
One fun option on the Pizza Hut India menu

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:37.020
is their new range of Momo Mia pizzas,

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.120
which are pan pizzas

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:42.180
with momos baked into the crust.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.521
Now, if you don't know what momos are,

00:12:43.521 --> 00:12:46.170
they're basically dumplings
from Nepal and Tibet.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.563
They're served all across India,

00:12:47.563 --> 00:12:50.580
and they've become huge favorites
for everybody over here.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:54.253
They've also given a
Schezwan sauce to the side,

00:12:54.253 --> 00:12:56.433
which is what you
typically eat with momos.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:58.913
Hm.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:00.752
No.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:04.440
That ain't right. I don't
see how this is working.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.806
I can't think of a single Italian

00:13:05.806 --> 00:13:07.372
who would put a pocket of ravioli

00:13:07.372 --> 00:13:10.080
on top of pizza and
then bake them together.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.210
And this is effectively what that is.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.900
We also have a range of
Flavour Fun personal pan pizzas

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:18.390
that you can get with
a host of new flavors.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:20.490
Starting off with classic corn.

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:23.400
Next up, we have the
classic onion and capsicum.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.230
Tandoori mushroom and corn.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:26.850
So, it looks similar to this,

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:29.460
but it used tandoori sauce
and the varied mushrooms.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.370
Next up, we have the classic
paneer, onion, and capsicum.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:35.100
Then we have the classic chicken sausage,

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.750
but personal-pan-sized.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.060
Next, we have the Italian
pepperoni and onion.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.785
And just a reminder that the pepperoni

00:13:40.785 --> 00:13:42.690
that they've used is chicken pepperoni.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:44.070
Tandoori chicken tikka and onion,

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.500
and the classic loaded chicken delight.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.192
Personally, [crickets chirping]

00:13:48.192 --> 00:13:50.250
I wouldn't order these pans.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:51.908
I would get the larger pizzas,

00:13:51.908 --> 00:13:53.766
'cause they tasted way better.

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:55.661
On top of set menu items,

00:13:55.661 --> 00:13:58.740
we can also customize our
pizzas in unique ways.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.870
For example, if you don't want
tomato sauce as your base,

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.780
you can sub it out for
creamy garlic Parmesan,

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.478
barbecue sauce, remember from before?

00:14:05.478 --> 00:14:08.503
Buffalo sauce, or a no-sauce option

00:14:08.503 --> 00:14:10.320
if you are a maniac.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.540
And if you want you can specify light,

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.070
regular, or extra sauce.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:16.053
Unfortunately, we can't change the sauces

00:14:16.053 --> 00:14:17.310
on our pizza bases,

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:19.783
but we have a bunch of custom toppings

00:14:19.783 --> 00:14:21.083
that you will not find in the US,

00:14:21.083 --> 00:14:23.983
like baby corn, sweet
corn, herbed veggies,

00:14:23.983 --> 00:14:26.843
spiced paneer, and veg kebab.

00:14:26.843 --> 00:14:28.350
And we also have exclusive toppings

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:29.490
you cannot get in India.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:32.548
For instance, we have
pepperoni, which is pork;

00:14:32.548 --> 00:14:34.557
our Italian sausage has pork;

00:14:34.557 --> 00:14:36.565
bacon, ah, I believe is pork;

00:14:36.565 --> 00:14:38.315
meatballs, beef and pork;

00:14:38.315 --> 00:14:39.728
ham, pork;

00:14:39.728 --> 00:14:41.920
and then beef;

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:42.753
and pork.

00:14:42.753 --> 00:14:44.978
Then the vegetables: We got white onion;

00:14:44.978 --> 00:14:46.770
we got pineapple, which is a fruit;

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:48.330
and we have banana
peppers, which I don't know

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.490
if it's a fruit or a
vegetable or a pepper.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.600
Are peppers fruit?

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:53.517
Whenever we have the
option of customizations

00:14:53.517 --> 00:14:55.650
on "Food Wars," we like
to combine all of our

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:59.460
exclusive ingredients to
make an India-only pizza.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:03.370
So this pizza has a Schezwan
base with baby corn,

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:07.863
veg kebab, spiced paneer,
and herbed veggies.

00:15:07.863 --> 00:15:09.870
It looks pretty gnarly, I'm not gonna lie,

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:11.561
but let's see how it tastes.

00:15:14.322 --> 00:15:15.510
Hm.

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.430
I can see why Pizza Hut didn't put this

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.600
officially on their menu,

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.120
'cause maybe the ingredients
don't go that well together,

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:25.260
but, hey, this is an
India-only Pizza Hut pizza,

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.670
and that means something.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:30.960
And, of course, we had to
create our own US-only pizza.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:35.490
So, the thin crispy base,
creamy garlic Parmesan sauce,

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:38.010
beef, bacon, white onion,

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:42.177
and everyone's favorite
vegetable, banana peppers.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.636
No!

00:15:46.636 --> 00:15:48.762
This looks like a cartoon pizza.

00:15:48.762 --> 00:15:50.049
Ah.

00:15:52.769 --> 00:15:54.180
OK, it's not bad.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.860
It's not great. I wouldn't get it.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.577
Yeah, it tastes like onion and bacon.

00:15:57.577 --> 00:15:58.410
Don't get this.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.460
Oop!

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:01.262
Pizza Hut has a bunch of sides.

00:16:01.262 --> 00:16:02.970
So, let's start off with the breads.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:05.441
First off, we have cheese garlic bread.

00:16:05.441 --> 00:16:09.210
Then we have spicy supreme
cheese garlic bread.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.352
It's basically cheese melted

00:16:10.352 --> 00:16:12.180
on top of a garlic bread baguette.

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:15.480
It's got some green chili
and some chopped onions.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.040
It's very delicious when it's hot.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:21.360
Mexican garlic breadsticks.
Oregano sprinkled on top,

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:24.360
some jalapeño, some
chopped olives, and onions.

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:25.500
It looks really delicious.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.870
Creamy garlic breadsticks.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.930
And finally we have garlic
breadsticks in a little packet

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.145
that says "GARLIC BREAD STIX."

00:16:33.145 --> 00:16:34.890
The US Pizza Hut only offers

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.600
regular breadsticks and cheese sticks.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.028
So, in fact, the only
actual exclusive side

00:16:39.028 --> 00:16:42.420
that we have in the US is fries.

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:43.860
We have a bunch of other sides,

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:47.223
including baked cheesy momos veg

00:16:47.223 --> 00:16:49.743
and baked cheesy momos non-veg.

00:16:50.924 --> 00:16:52.890
Whew. That's a potent smell.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.690
You know what?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.550
It's not half bad.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:58.140
Next up we have potato poppers,

00:16:58.140 --> 00:16:59.700
which are pretty much Tater Tots.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.595
We have the Indi Rockin Roll veg

00:17:02.595 --> 00:17:05.750
and the Indi Rockin Roll non-veg.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:06.600
This is basically a roll,

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.600
but I like how the wrap is kind of thin.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.870
Again, it's quite good.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.360
Next up, we have the zesty paneer pocket

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.467
and the zesty chicken pocket.

00:17:17.467 --> 00:17:19.710
These are pretty much like pizza pockets.

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:22.920
There's some mint mayo, some
normal mayo, some cream cheese,

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:25.470
chicken, and jalapeños.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:27.519
We have jalapeño poppers.

00:17:27.519 --> 00:17:29.738
I imagine they're just filled with cheese

00:17:29.738 --> 00:17:30.840
and some jalapeño bits.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:33.300
Oh, ugh, I did not
expect that consistency.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:36.270
And that brings us to an
old classic: chicken wings.

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:38.100
Spicy baked chicken wings.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:41.320
So I suppose they're a
healthier alternative?

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:44.250
WingStreet wings.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.083
Yes!

00:17:45.083 --> 00:17:47.160
Both traditional and boneless.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.234
You can get them in the following flavors.

00:17:49.234 --> 00:17:52.285
Lemon pepper. Oh, let's go, lemon pepper.

00:17:52.285 --> 00:17:53.340
I usually don't like lemon pepper,

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.180
but these are pretty good.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:55.365
Ooh, honey barbecue.

00:17:55.365 --> 00:17:58.530
Ugh, these things are like condensation.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.410
Ah, ooh, the medium Buffalo.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.703
Ooh, Cajun style!

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.610
Eh, just OK.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:08.160
Spicy garlic. What?

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.620
Naked. That's wings with nothing on it.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.048
Why would you do that? I don't know.

00:18:12.048 --> 00:18:13.950
Buffalo Burnin' Hot.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:16.030
Three flames!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:18.810
Mm, this should be your medium.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:20.882
Oh, wait!

00:18:20.882 --> 00:18:22.440
Yeah, OK.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.520
Sweet chili.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.412
Am I sweating? I feel like I'm sweating.

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:29.580
They're all just eh. You
know, I mean, I like wings.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.650
Maybe my wing standards are too high.

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:34.316
Garlic Parmesan. Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho!

00:18:35.272 --> 00:18:36.130
[sighs]

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:39.023
Oh, my God!

00:18:39.023 --> 00:18:41.640
I mean, the sauce is like
pasta sauce. It's really thick.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.600
It's got a lot of flavor to it,

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:45.450
but it's just, like, sitting in the sauce,

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.640
so either you get a
mouthful of sauce or none.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:51.810
And these come in portions
of six, 12, 18, or 36.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:53.730
And next up on the menu,

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:56.610
you can also find a range of pastas,

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.861
starting with the creamy mushroom.

00:18:58.861 --> 00:19:00.810
[sauce squishing]

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:03.819
You know what? If I have to
listen to this, so will you all.

00:19:03.819 --> 00:19:07.050
[sauce squishing]

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:08.855
Just get some in the boom mic.

00:19:08.855 --> 00:19:11.396
[sauce squishing]

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.120
Decent pasta for a fast-food restaurant.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:17.432
They have a cheesy comfort veg pasta

00:19:17.432 --> 00:19:20.100
and a cheesy comfort chicken pasta.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:21.450
It's too gooey.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:24.067
We have the spiced Tomato Twist veg pasta

00:19:24.067 --> 00:19:26.883
and the spiced Tomato Twist non-veg pasta.

00:19:26.883 --> 00:19:30.182
If you come to Pizza Hut to order pasta,

00:19:30.182 --> 00:19:31.980
I hope we never cross paths.

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.930
Nikhil, you have no idea.

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:36.540
We absolutely love our
carbs in this country.

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:37.560
And as you can see,

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:41.130
we have bowls and bowls of
carbs that we call pasta.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:44.536
You can get four exclusive
oven-baked pastas

00:19:44.536 --> 00:19:47.646
at pa -- pasta hut. At Pizza Hut.

00:19:48.621 --> 00:19:51.180
I'm not eating any of these.
They all taste terrible.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:52.310
All right? The end.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:56.370
You can get a oven-baked
chicken Alfredo. Don't get this.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:57.960
Or, if you don't like chicken,

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.720
you can just get cheesy Alfredo.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.240
And then, of course, we have
the Italian meats pasta,

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:04.920
which is pepperoni and Italian sausage.

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:08.707
I mean, oh, Italy. Oh, Italy.

00:20:08.707 --> 00:20:09.960
I'm so sorry.

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:13.670
And, lastly, the oven-baked veggie pasta.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.411
I mean, this is a doorstop.

00:20:17.855 --> 00:20:21.090
I can't stand the Pizza Hut pasta.

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:22.260
I cannot stand it.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:25.281
You see the sauces. You
know what time it is.

00:20:25.281 --> 00:20:26.640
Sauce talk.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:29.850
Starting down here, get
yourself blue cheese sauce,

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:32.250
then get ranch.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.320
Ooh, a garlic sauce.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.510
We can have a honey barbecue sauce,

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:40.122
a medium Buffalo sauce,
and a side of marinara,

00:20:40.122 --> 00:20:42.180
just for dipping your breadsticks.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:46.140
And also icing, the Cinnabon
icing for the Cinnabuns.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.167
And there's a note that says,

00:20:47.167 --> 00:20:50.940
"I really want to see Joe dipping
some pizza in the frosting

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:52.430
and eat it."

00:20:54.071 --> 00:20:55.246
[sighs]

00:20:56.129 --> 00:20:57.435
Give me this.

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.760
Oh!

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:07.082
Actually ...

00:21:07.082 --> 00:21:09.332
At first I was like, yuck,
but this is kind of good.

00:21:09.332 --> 00:21:11.820
And now on to dips. You dips---s.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:15.020
First off, we have tomato ketchup. Ha ha.

00:21:17.921 --> 00:21:18.990
[crew laughing]

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:21.150
Then we have a mayonnaise.

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:23.130
Fun fact: It's veg mayonnaise,

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.600
doesn't have any egg, because a huge

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:28.290
population of this country
is pure vegetarians,

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.940
which means that they don't eat anything

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:32.370
from an animal, even egg.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:34.140
Then we have a cheese dip.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:36.450
And finally, it's a Schezwan sauce.

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:37.920
And they serve it with the momos,

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:39.611
they serve it with a
bunch of other things.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.273
Yeah.

00:21:44.273 --> 00:21:46.560
We got desserts you're
not gonna find in India.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:49.560
That includes, down here,
the cinnamon sticks.

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:53.010
They're like breadsticks, only cinnamony.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:55.754
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho.

00:21:55.754 --> 00:21:57.690
Get your mind out of the gutter.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.434
And moving on, we have here are the

00:21:59.434 --> 00:22:02.310
Cinnabon mini cinnamon rolls.

00:22:02.310 --> 00:22:06.000
This is the triple chocolate brownie.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.037
If I had to guess, 2 pounds.

00:22:08.037 --> 00:22:10.779
What do we got here? The
ultimate chocolate chip cookie.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:13.800
Right?

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:15.490
This is like a Frisbee.

00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:19.980
And for all you sweetie pies
out there with sweet tooths,

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:22.410
here are India's exclusive desserts,

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:26.582
starting with a choco lava cake, baby!

00:22:26.582 --> 00:22:27.732
Ooh!

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:29.940
Molten.

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:33.690
The choco lava cake in
Domino's? Much better.

00:22:33.690 --> 00:22:35.160
Next up, you get a whole
range of ice cream.

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:36.360
Some Kwality Wall's,

00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:39.240
one of India's biggest
ice cream manufacturers.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:42.660
You can get a tiny tub of
Choco-Tastic Supreme Sundae.

00:22:42.660 --> 00:22:45.240
Then you can get a Cornetto, a cone.

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:47.920
Super delicious. And I
really love the end of this,

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:49.853
because it's just a block of chocolate,

00:22:49.853 --> 00:22:52.436
and I used to fight over
this with my friends.

00:22:52.436 --> 00:22:55.410
Then you get a Magnum.
Everybody loves a Magnum.

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:59.280
And finally, you can even get
a family pack of ice cream.

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:00.480
Soda!

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:03.270
Last exclusive are, of course, the drinks.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:06.090
Both countries have Pepsi,
but the Pizza Hut in the US

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:10.111
you can also get wild
cherry Pepsi, orange Crush,

00:23:10.111 --> 00:23:11.730
Mountain Dew, baby!

00:23:11.730 --> 00:23:13.621
Sierra Mist, which they didn't have,

00:23:13.621 --> 00:23:15.660
and Aquafina.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:18.330
Here in Pizza Hut India,
our exclusive drink options

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:22.410
are Pepsi, 7Up, Mirinda, and Pepsi black.

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:24.450
They also serve an iced
tea at the restaurant,

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:26.370
but they don't deliver it, unfortunately.

00:23:26.370 --> 00:23:28.403
I would've gone for the iced tea.

00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:33.510
All right, now let's take a
look at Pizza Hut's pricing,

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:35.587
particularly some clever marketing tricks

00:23:35.587 --> 00:23:37.407
they're using to make you
believe you're getting

00:23:37.407 --> 00:23:39.870
more value for money
than you actually are.

00:23:39.870 --> 00:23:43.385
In the US, a medium cheese
pizza on the pan crust

00:23:43.385 --> 00:23:46.500
will cost you $13.49.

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:49.093
In India, a medium Margherita
pizza will cost you

00:23:49.093 --> 00:23:53.641
319 rupees, which is
currently 3.93 US dollars.

00:23:53.641 --> 00:23:56.872
That means over here you
are paying 11.9 cents

00:23:56.872 --> 00:23:58.950
per square inch of pizza.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:00.030
While over here in India,

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:03.930
you're just paying 4.4 cents
per square inch of pizza.

00:24:03.930 --> 00:24:07.979
That makes the US pizza
170% more expensive.

00:24:07.979 --> 00:24:09.750
Generally with pizza, the more you buy,

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:10.830
the cheaper it gets.

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:15.809
A US large has a surface
area of 153.9 square inches

00:24:15.809 --> 00:24:18.630
and costs $15.49.

00:24:18.630 --> 00:24:21.720
That brings the cost per
square inch down to 10 cents,

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:24.780
making it 15% cheaper than the medium.

00:24:24.780 --> 00:24:28.530
Ladies and gentlemen, it's
time for pizza pop quiz!

00:24:28.530 --> 00:24:30.832
Which has the higher surface area,

00:24:30.832 --> 00:24:35.100
one medium pizza or two personal pizzas?

00:24:35.100 --> 00:24:39.000
If you said two personal
pizzas, congratulations!

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:40.200
You're an idiot.

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:42.620
Because when it comes to
calculating the surface area

00:24:42.620 --> 00:24:45.043
of a circle, small changes in diameter

00:24:45.043 --> 00:24:47.970
can create huge differences
in surface area.

00:24:47.970 --> 00:24:50.940
On the Pizza Hut India website,
you can get a combo offer

00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:54.570
of two personal pan pizzas for rupees 279.

00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:58.050
However, a medium pizza
costs pretty much the same.

00:24:58.050 --> 00:25:01.140
But I guess if you want two
different flavors of pizza,

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:03.532
it makes sense to go with the combo.

00:25:05.865 --> 00:25:07.971
In this medium cheese pan-crust pizza,

00:25:07.971 --> 00:25:10.080
it is 1,940 calories,

00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:15.075
79 grams of total fat, 33
grams of saturated fat,

00:25:15.075 --> 00:25:19.512
224 grams of carbs, and
the sodium, oh, boy,

00:25:19.512 --> 00:25:22.530
3,480 milligrams.

00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:25.485
A medium Margherita pizza
in India will cost you

00:25:25.485 --> 00:25:28.068
1,377 calories,

00:25:28.068 --> 00:25:30.613
total fat 40.29 grams,

00:25:30.613 --> 00:25:33.363
of which saturates are 14.7 grams,

00:25:33.363 --> 00:25:35.529
carbohydrates, 192 grams,

00:25:35.529 --> 00:25:40.087
and 2,717 milligrams of sodium.

00:25:40.087 --> 00:25:40.920
Yikes.

00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:43.140
Now, the American stats look a lot worse,

00:25:43.140 --> 00:25:44.898
but I do want to point out that our medium

00:25:44.898 --> 00:25:46.380
is much larger than India's.

00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:48.870
So if you break it down per square inch,

00:25:48.870 --> 00:25:51.502
you'll see that the US version

00:25:51.502 --> 00:25:53.543
does have more fat and more saturated fat,

00:25:53.543 --> 00:25:55.811
but India's pizza actually contains

00:25:55.811 --> 00:25:58.800
more calories, carbs, and sodium.

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:02.730
But what about the most calorific
item on the Indian menu?

00:26:02.730 --> 00:26:04.923
If you really want to mess up your day,

00:26:04.923 --> 00:26:09.274
you have to order the medium
veg Surprise Kebab pizza

00:26:09.274 --> 00:26:12.270
with veg-kebab-stuffed crust.

00:26:12.270 --> 00:26:14.836
A whole one of these pizzas will contain

00:26:14.836 --> 00:26:17.969
2,673 calories.

00:26:17.969 --> 00:26:21.277
That's 133.65% of your daily

00:26:21.277 --> 00:26:23.452
caloric-intake allowance.

00:26:23.452 --> 00:26:25.170
Oh, my God.

00:26:25.170 --> 00:26:28.387
OK, the calories are high,
but the sodium is even higher.

00:26:28.387 --> 00:26:32.520
There is 6,344 milligrams
of sodium in here,

00:26:32.520 --> 00:26:37.355
which is 275% of your daily
recommended allowance.

00:26:37.355 --> 00:26:40.110
What about the most calorific
pizza in the US, you ask?

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:44.160
Well, that would be a large
pan-crusted Meat Lover's,

00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:45.960
which this isn't.

00:26:45.960 --> 00:26:48.136
So imagine it bigger and thicker. OK.

00:26:48.136 --> 00:26:50.752
An entire one of these contains a whopping

00:26:50.752 --> 00:26:53.394
3,570 calories.

00:26:53.394 --> 00:26:56.220
That's 178% of your daily allowance.

00:26:56.220 --> 00:26:59.610
And the sodium is even
worse than that of India's.

00:26:59.610 --> 00:27:03.540
There's 7,150 milligrams
of sodium in here.

00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:06.640
That is 298%

00:27:06.640 --> 00:27:09.065
your daily recommended amount.

00:27:09.065 --> 00:27:11.850
Also, this pizza is
not particularly round.

00:27:11.850 --> 00:27:13.158
It's shaped like a --

00:27:13.158 --> 00:27:15.510
one, two, three, four,
five, six -- hexagon.

00:27:15.510 --> 00:27:16.785
Look at that.

00:27:17.918 --> 00:27:21.070
Just a fun fact in case
you're a geometry nerd.

